        "passageTitle": "Questions 158-160 refer to the following press release.",
        "passageText": "FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE Contact: Sherylin Stevens, sstevens@tearsoncorp.ca CALGARY (2 November) ------- Yves Vernier, the Chief Information Officer of the Tearson\nCorporation, announced on Monday that 200 robots will soon appear in Tearson’s grocery\nstores. The robots, which are all named Bailey, will be used to locate areas where boxes\nor bottles have fallen and broken, spilling cereal, juice, or other substances onto the floor.\nThe robots will report the spills so that the locations can be cleaned by store employees\nbefore they become safety hazards.\nThe robots were tested in Calgary, where Tearson’s head office is located. During the\neighteen-month pilot program me, store managers consistently gave the robots high marks.\nAlthough the robots have been used in the company’s warehouses for several years, this\nwill be their first time working in stores and interacting with customers. All Tearson stores\nshould have the robots by the beginning of December.\nFor more information, visit Tearson Corporation at www.tearsoncorporation.ca.",
